G3120.b:
⟪μαλακός⟫, -ή, -όν,
[in LXX: ⟦Proverbs 25:15|Pr 25:15⟧ (⁨רַךְ⁩) ⟦Proverbs 26:22|Pr 26:22⟧ (⁨כְּמִתְלַהֲמִים⁩)*;] ⟪soft⟫;
⟪1.⟫ prop., to the touch (opp. to σκληρός): of clothing, pl., ⟦Matthew 11:8|Mt 11:8⟧, ⟦Luke 7:25|Lk 7:25⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of persons and their mode of living;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪mild⟫, ⟪gentle⟫;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪soft⟫, ⟪effeminate⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 6:9|I Co 6:9⟧ (prob. in obscene sense, cf. Deiss., LAE, 1504; MM, xvi; Zorell, s.v.).†

G3128.b:
⟪Μανασσῆς⟫, -ῆ, ὁ (Heb. ⁨מְנַשֶּׁה⁩), ⟪Manasseh⟫;
⟪1.⟫
	⟪(a)⟫ the first-born son of Joseph;
	⟪(b)⟫ the tribe which bore his name: ⟦Revelation 7:6|Re 7:6⟧.
⟪2.⟫ King of Judah: ⟦Matthew 1:10|Mt 1:10⟧.†

G3173.b:
⟪μέγας⟫, μεγάλη, μέγα,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨גָּדוֹל⁩, also for ⁨רַב⁩, ⁨מַרְבֶּה⁩ (incl. μείζων), ⁨רֹב⁩ (μέγιστος);] ⟪great⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of external form, bodily size, measure, extent: λίθος, ⟦Matthew 2:60|Mt 2:60⟧; δράκων, ⟦Revelation 12:3|Re 12:3⟧; ἰχθῦς, ⟦John 21:11|Jo 21:11⟧; πόλις, ⟦Revelation 11:8|Re 11:8⟧; μάχαιρα, ⟦Revelation 6:4|Re 6:4⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ Of intensity and degree: δύναμις, ⟦Acts 4:33|Ac 4:33⟧; φόβος, ⟦Mark 4:41|Mk 4:41⟧; ἀγάπη, ⟦John 15:13|Jo 15:13⟧; ἄνεμος, ⟦John 6:18|Jo 6:18⟧; κραυγή, ⟦Acts 23:9|Ac 23:9⟧; φῶς, ⟦Matthew 4:16|Mt 4:16⟧; πυρετός, ⟦Luke 4:38|Lk 4:38⟧; θλίψις, ⟦Matthew 24:21|Mt 24:21⟧.
⟪3.⟫ Of rank;
	⟪(a)⟫ of persons: θεός (MM, xvi), ⟦Titus 2:13|Tit 2:13⟧; Ἄρτεμις, ⟦Acts 19:27|Ac 19:27⟧; compar. (v. infr.), ⟦Matthew 18:1|Mt 18:1⟧ (cf. Dalman, Words, 113 f.); neut. for masc. (Bl., §32, 1), ⟦Matthew 12:6|Mt 12:6⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of things: ἁμαρτία, ⟦John 19:11|Jo 19:11⟧; μυστήριον, ⟦Ephesians 5:32|Eph 5:32⟧; = μεγίστη (v. infr., and cf. Field, Notes, 16 f.), ⟦Matthew 22:36|Mt 22:36⟧; compar. for superl. (M, Pr., 78), ⟦1 Corinthians 13:13|I Co 13:13⟧.
⟪4.⟫
	⟪(a)⟫ Compar., μείζων: ⟦Matthew 11:11|Mt 11:11⟧ ⟦Matthew 23:17|23:17⟧, al.; neut. pl., μείζονα, contr. μείζω, ⟦John 1:51|Jo 1:51⟧; double compar., μειζότερος (M, Pr., 236; Bl., § 11, 4), ⟦3 John 1:4|III Jo 4⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ superl., μέγιστος (Deiss., BS, 365), ⟦2 Peter 1:4|II Pe 1:4⟧.

G3195.b:
⟪μέλλω⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦Job 3:8|Jb 3:8⟧ (⁨עָתִיד⁩) ⟦Job 19:25|19:25⟧ (⁨אַחֲרוֹן⁩); elsewhere for fut., and freq. in Wi, II, IV Mac;] ⟪to be about⟫ to be or do;
⟪1.⟫ c. inf. (Bl., § 62, 4; 68, 2; M, Pr., 114);
	⟪(a)⟫ of intending or being about to do of one's own free will: c. inf. praes., ⟦Matthew 2:13|Mt 2:13⟧, ⟦Luke 10:1|Lk 10:1⟧, ⟦Acts 3:3|Ac 3:3⟧ ⟦Acts 5:35|5:35⟧, ⟦Hebrews 8:5|He 8:5⟧, ⟦2 Peter 1:12|II Pe 1:12⟧ (Field, Notes, 240), al.; c. inf. aor. (Bl., § 58, 3), ⟦Acts 12:6|Ac 12:6⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:16|Re 3:16⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of compulsion, necessity or certainty: c. inf. praes., ⟦Matthew 16:27|Mt 16:27⟧, ⟦Luke 9:31|Lk 9:31⟧, ⟦John 6:71|Jo 6:71⟧, ⟦Romans 4:24|Ro 4:24⟧, al.; c. inf. aor., ⟦Romans 8:18|Ro 8:18⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:23|Ga 3:23⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:2|Re 3:2⟧ ⟦Revelation 12:4|12:4⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Ptcp., ὁ μέλλων: absol., ⟦Romans 8:38|Ro 8:38⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:22|I Co 3:22⟧; τὰ μ., ⟦Colossians 2:17|Col 2:17⟧; εἰς τὸ μ. (Field, Notes, 65); c. subst., ⟦Matthew 3:7|Mt 3:7⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:32|12:32⟧ (ὁ αἰὼν ὁ μ.; LXX for ⁨עַד⁩), ⟦Acts 24:25|Ac 24:25⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 4:8|I Ti 4:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:5|He 2:5⟧, al.
